#: ../../tutorial/04_keypads.rst:60
msgid "A ``CallbackData`` factory is **not** currently shipped with aiorubi — the package exposes ``Command``, ``CommandStart``, ``CommandObject``, ``StateFilter``, ``MagicData``, ``ExceptionTypeFilter``, ``ExceptionMessageFilter``, the combinators ``and_f`` / ``or_f`` / ``invert_f`` and the ``Filter`` base class. For typed callback data, route on ``aux_data.button_id`` values directly (as shown above), or write your own small factory filter on top of :class:`~aiorubi.filters.base.Filter`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/04_keypads.rst:69
msgid "Filtering on the button id is the simplest way to route clicks. The full filter toolkit is described in :doc:`/guide/filter`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tutorial/04_keypads.rst:74
msgid "``InlineMessage`` is *not* a ``Message``. It has ``sender_id``, ``chat_id``, ``aux_data`` and an ``aux_data.button_id``, but no ``text`` and no ``reply()`` shortcuts. Use ``await call.answer(...)`` to respond."
msgstr ""

